%% UC-13 — Submit weekly SRHI check-in
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor P as Participant
    participant F as Flutter App
    participant B as Backend (srhiService)
    participant M as MongoDB

    Note over B,M: Windows are pre-generated, not computed on the fly. SRHI is<br/>unconditional — no per-study admin toggle — so every habit creation triggers<br/>srhiService.generateWindows, inserting 4 weekly srhi_responses rows (week 1 =<br/>creation day + ~5s), independent of questionnaire_assignments. Item text/scale<br/>(1-7 slider) is hardcoded in app/utils/srhi.js, not read from the questionnaires<br/>collection. A ~5 s FCM push (data.screen=habits) then deep-links the<br/>participant straight into My Habits (see UC-35 / UC-15).

    F->>B: GET /api/v1/srhi/due
    B->>M: Find pending windows (submittedAt=null) whose<br/>scheduledFor is within the 3-day submission window
    M-->>B: due windows
    B-->>F: [{intentionId, weekNumber, scheduledFor}]
    P->>F: Answer 12 SRHI items (1-7 scale)
    F->>B: POST /api/v1/srhi/{intentionId}/week/{weekNumber} {items}
    B->>B: Compute score = mean(srhi_1..srhi_12)
    B->>M: upsert(srhi_responses, key {intentionId, weekNumber})
    M-->>B: stored
    B-->>F: 201 {score}
    F->>B: GET /api/v1/srhi/{intentionId}/trajectory
    B-->>F: score trajectory for this intention
